Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/gregbook/rpng2-x.c
Line: 2077
Function: is_number
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: isdigit() is called with *p of type char, which may be negative on platforms where char is signed. The ctype macros require either EOF or an unsigned char value. Passing a negative value can cause an out-of-bounds table access in the ctype implementation (undefined behavior). Cast to (unsigned char) before calling isdigit.

